---
// HOMEPAGE — V3 lean Sevenson architecture, rebuilt 2026-08-25.
//
// Section order is docs/ASEPTACLEAN-CODEX-HOMEPAGE-BRIEF-V3-LEAN-SEVENSON.md §6, which the brief
// itself declares supersedes the earlier section-order instructions in
// docs/ASEPTACLEAN-CODEX-HOMEPAGE-REBUILD-BRIEF-SEVENSON.md and docs/30-WEBSITE-MASTER-SPEC.md
// §36.1 wherever they conflict. It is an explicit current owner decision (AGENTS.md §1 rank 2)
// and therefore outranks the master spec's thirteen-beat list (rank 5). Recorded in
// docs/05-DECISIONS-LOG.md.
//
//   01 Utility + Main Navigation   (StatusRibbon + Header, in BaseLayout)
//   02 Hero
//   03 What We Handle
//   04 The Property Condition Changes the Work
//   05 Operating Evidence / How Aseptaclean Works
//   06 Final CTA
//   07 Footer                      (in BaseLayout)
//
// WHY THIS IS A REDUCTION, NOT A RESTYLE. The 2026-08-25 audit measured the previous build at
// 11,704px / 1,678 words / eight H2s / five repeats of one H2-left-content-right composition,
// with two photographs below the hero. V3 §0 rules that the correction is to remove structure,
// not to make the same page prettier. Eleven rendered sections became five.
//
// SECTIONS MERGED IN THIS PASS — content absorbed, not discarded:
//   ConditionRecognition + ServiceFeatures  → WhatWeHandle
//       V3 §10: the homepage does not need two routing systems for the same idea. One
//       photographic section now does both jobs — "that looks like my situation" and "yes,
//       Aseptaclean handles this".
//   ScopeExplanation → ConditionChangesWork
//       V3 §11: the standalone "A Clear Scope Before Work Begins" section is deleted and its
//       load-bearing sentence ("The scope is defined before work begins") is absorbed into the
//       differentiation section, which was already making the same argument.
//   HandoffRecord + OperatorAccountability → OperatingEvidence
//       V3 §12: one concentrated credibility movement instead of a record band, a founder
//       section with an empty bordered photo slot, and a generic trust block.
//
// SECTIONS REMOVED FROM `/`, CONTENT PRESERVED ELSEWHERE — V3 §§7, 13, 14, 15:
//   CostAndScope   → the cost DRIVERS and doc 27 §7's $195 assessment framing already render on
//                    every service page through ServicePricing, and on /private-residence-reset/.
//                    Nothing sitewide is lost. AGENTS.md §4 is untouched: no price figure moved,
//                    appeared, or changed anywhere in this pass.
//   ConfidenceAndFit → MOVED to /services/, which V3 §14 names as a correct home for fit and
//                    boundaries. homepage.excludedScope and homepage.qualification rendered
//                    NOWHERE else in the build, so deleting the section outright would have
//                    deleted the site's only sitewide exclusion list. The component file is
//                    unchanged; only its call site moved.
//                    POINTER UPDATED 2026-08-26: ConfidenceAndFit.astro no longer exists. The
//                    /services/ rebuild replaced it with ServiceScopeBoundary.astro, which
//                    renders the same three sources — homepage.qualification,
//                    homepage.excludedScope and legal.scopeDisclaimer — verbatim and unedited.
//                    The sentence above still holds: those two arrays render on exactly one
//                    route, and that route is still /services/.
//   FAQ           → still the whole of /faq/, which emits its own FAQPage JSON-LD. The homepage
//                    FAQPage node is removed with the section: schema must not describe content
//                    a visitor cannot see (docs/21-CLAIMS-AND-COMPLIANCE-LAW.md §6.1).
//
// PRESERVED DELIBERATELY: canonical, robots, sitemap membership, redirects, the lead endpoint,
// service-area generation, schema identity, and every publication gate. No route changed, no
// gated service became visible, and no regulated future service is named.
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ConditionChangesWork from "@components/ConditionChangesWork.astro";
import FinalCTA from "@components/FinalCTA.astro";
import Hero from "@components/Hero.astro";
import OperatingEvidence from "@components/OperatingEvidence.astro";
import WhatWeHandle from "@components/WhatWeHandle.astro";
import { homepage, site } from "@data/site";

// The Service nodes describe homepage.serviceCards. The LocalBusiness node remains defined once
// in src/components/SeoHead.astro; do not re-add a business node here.
//
// CORRECTION 2026-08-26 — the claim this comment used to make is FALSE and was left standing for
// a day. It read: "WhatWeHandle still renders those three families, so schema and visible copy
// cannot drift." They have drifted, and by design on both sides:
//
//   serviceCards  Detailed cleaning · Complex property cleanup · Animal & organic condition cleaning
//   WhatWeHandle  Overwhelming contents & hoarding · Neglected & heavily soiled properties ·
//                 Estate, move-out & property transitions
//
// Those are three CONDITIONS a visitor recognises, not the three service families, and the animal
// / organic family is deliberately absent from the visible page — WhatWeHandle's own header
// comment records why (its only route ships `noindex`, and a gated service is not exposed here).
// So `/` currently emits a Service node for a family the page does not describe or link to.
//
// NOT changed in this pass, deliberately. Deleting a Service node is a schema/representation
// decision affecting how the site's services are described, and the same string also ships on
// /services/ and /specialty-cleaning/, so a homepage-only edit would make the three disagree.
// Raised for owner review instead; see docs/05-DECISIONS-LOG.md, 2026-08-26. The second reason it
// needs a decision rather than a tidy-up: that node's `description` is the only place on `/` where
// the "organic pathogen endorsement" wording appears, and AGENTS.md §3 holds every insurance and
// endorsement claim release-gated until the wording is verified against a current COI.
const serviceSchemas = homepage.serviceCards.map((card) => ({
  "@type": "Service",
  serviceType: card.title,
  description: card.detail,
  provider: { "@id": new URL("/#business", site.urls.site).href },
  areaServed: site.location.cities.map((name) => ({
    "@type": "City",
    name
  }))
}));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Deep Cleaning & Complex Property Cleanup | San Jose | Aseptaclean"
  description="Deep cleaning, move-out cleaning, hoarding and estate cleanouts in the South Bay & Peninsula. Written scope first. Nothing removed without your approval."
  canonicalPath="/"
  schema={serviceSchemas}
>
  <Hero />
  <WhatWeHandle />
  <ConditionChangesWork />
  <OperatingEvidence />
  <FinalCTA />
</BaseLayout>
